  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "domain": "Education",
  "statement": "Design a database schema for a university registration system. Each Student has an ID, name, and email, and can enroll in many Courses; each Course can have many enrolled Students. Resolve this many-to-many relationship using an Enrollment table that tracks the enrolled_at date and grade. Every Course is taught by one Instructor, while an Instructor can teach many Courses.",
  "deliverables": [
    "Identify the core tables and assign Primary Keys.",
    "Resolve any many-to-many relationships with a join table.",
    "Set Crow's Foot cardinalities on each link."
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Remember to add a Primary Key (PK) attribute to every entity.",
    "Enrollment sits between Student and Course: Student (1) -> Enrollment (N) and Course (1) -> Enrollment (N).",
    "Instructor (1) -> Course (N) models the teaching assignment."
  ],
